  "label": "The text 'if they steal this one' maps to Gordon Ramsay as the entity being referred to.",
  "description": "The phrase 'if they steal this one' is a hyperbolic statement implying that if someone takes Gordon Ramsay (or his reputation, status, or something he represents), the speaker will react with extreme frustration. The visual material of Gordon Ramsay, with his angry expression and confrontational posture, is mapped onto the textual entity 'this one' to signify that he is the object of the hypothetical theft. This mapping relies on the visual representation of Ramsay's persona as a valuable, irreplaceable, or highly prized entity in the context of celebrity culture and his public image.",
